@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`

-- g6-payment.l4: ss.48-51.  Payment within 30 days of the payment demand (s.48), the shekel interest and
-- arrears fees of a late payment (s.49, the amount a named refusal unless the caller supplies it), payment by
-- instalments (s.50), and the destination of the money (s.51, inert).
--
-- Clock convention for the regulative rules here: `AT 0` is the day the payment demand was delivered (or is
-- treated as delivered under s.44(d)); an event `AT k` happened k days after it.
--
-- Periods owned here (PLAN section (d)):
--   P31, s.48: 30 days from delivery of the payment demand: a deadline for doing something, kind D.
--     IL s.10(a); IL s.10(c) applied (ruling 4); the alternative without it is callable.
--   P32, s.50(a): "not more than 12 monthly payments": a count, kind Q, outside IL s.10.
--   P45, s.49: the period of the delay, from the day after the payment fell due to the day of payment: kind V,
--     a stretch of days, IL s.10(c) not applied (it moves the end of a deadline, and nothing here is one).
--
-- Not in the sources: the Interest and Linkage Law's rates and mechanics (outside the scope); whether a payment
-- period stated in the demand governs over s.48's 30 days (trap T16).

§ `Chapter 6: administrative enforcement measures`

§§ `Subchapter A: imposing a financial sanction`

§§§ `ss 48 to 51: the acts`

@desc The acts of ss.48 to 50: paying the sanction (in time, or late with interest and arrears fees) and the Commissioner's allowing payment by instalments; the first field says who performs each act
DECLARE `Act under ss 48 to 51` IS ONE OF
    `pay the financial sanction`
        HAS `performed by the paying violator` IS A Party
            `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the financial sanction together with the interest and arrears fees`
        HAS `performed by the violator paying late` IS A Party
            `the amount paid late` IS A NUMBER
    `allow payment of the financial sanction by instalments`
        HAS `performed by the officer allowing instalments` IS A Party

§§§ `s 48: the date for payment`

-- src:378 | {{ח:סעיף|48|המועד לתשלום העיצום הכספי}}
-- src:379 | {{ח:ת}} על המפר לשלם את העיצום הכספי בתוך 30 ימים מיום מסירת דרישת התשלום כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 44|בסעיף 44}}.
-- "The violator shall pay the financial sanction within 30 days of the day the payment demand was delivered
-- as stated in s.44."  Kind D (a deadline for doing something): IL s.10(a), the day of delivery not counted,
-- and IL s.10(c) applied (ruling 4).  For a violator who made no representations the payment demand is the
-- notice of intention treated as one under s.44(d), delivered at the end of the s.43 period (g6-notice-and-hearing),
-- so the two periods run in turn and he has up to 60 days from the notice (trap T16).
@ref s.48 (src:379)
@export The last day for paying a financial sanction: 30 days from the day the payment demand was delivered (or is treated as delivered), moved past days of rest, recess or holiday
GIVEN delivered IS A DATE @desc The day the payment demand was delivered, or is treated as delivered under s.44(d), as an ISO 8601 date
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday under an enactment for the years the question touches, as a list of dates (never computed)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` delivered calendar MEANS
    `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` delivered `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)

@ref s.48 (src:379)
GIVEN delivered IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand, without s 10(c)` delivered MEANS
    `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` delivered

-- Trap T16 (fork F-PERIOD): s.42(b)(2) and s.44(b)(1) say the notice and the demand state "the period for
-- payment", and s.48 says 30 days.  Taken: s.48's 30 days govern whatever the demand states, because s.48 is
-- the provision that fixes when the violator "shall pay"; the demand "states" the period, it does not fix it.
-- The alternative: a period stated in the demand governs when there is one.
@ref s.44(b)(1), s.48 (src:379)
GIVEN delivered IS A DATE
      `the period for payment the demand states, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 48 — the last day for payment, when a period stated in the demand governs` delivered `the period for payment the demand states, in days` calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period for payment the demand states, in days`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` delivered calendar
    WHEN JUST stated THEN `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` stated `days from` delivered `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)

@ref s.48 (src:379)
GIVEN delivered IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 48 — the number of days from the delivery of the demand to the last day for payment` delivered calendar MEANS
    (Day (`s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` delivered calendar)) MINUS (Day delivered)

-- Is a day inside the payment period?  A payment made on the day the demand is delivered is "within 30 days" of it (fork
-- F-ACTDAY, as at s.43): the day of delivery or later, and the last day or earlier; the last day is inside.
@ref s.48 (src:379)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      delivered IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48 — the day` day `is within the period for payment that runs from` delivered `with` calendar MEANS
        (delivered AT MOST day)
    AND (day AT MOST `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` delivered calendar)

-- Fork F-ACTDAY: the strict reading, the period beginning the day AFTER delivery.
@ref s.48 (src:379)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      delivered IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 48 — counting the day after delivery as the first day, the day` day `is within the period for payment that runs from` delivered `with` calendar MEANS
    `s 8, s 10 — the date` day `is inside the period beginning on` (`s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` delivered) `and ending on` (`s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` delivered calendar)

§§§ `s 49: shekel interest and arrears fees on a late payment`

-- src:381 | {{ח:סעיף|49|ריבית שקלית ודמי פיגורים}}
-- src:382 | {{ח:ת}} לא שילם המפר עיצום כספי במועד, ייווספו עליו, לתקופת הפיגור, ריבית שקלית ודמי פיגורים, עד לתשלומו, ויחולו הוראות {{ח:חיצוני|חוק פסיקת ריבית והצמדה|חוק פסיקת ריבית והצמדה}}, בשינויים המחויבים; {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|בפרק זה}} –
-- src:383 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”דמי פיגורים“ ו”ריבית שקלית“ – כהגדרתם {{ח:חיצוני|חוק פסיקת ריבית והצמדה|בחוק פסיקת ריבית והצמדה}};
-- src:384 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”חוק פסיקת ריבית והצמדה“ – {{ח:חיצוני|חוק פסיקת ריבית והצמדה|חוק פסיקת ריבית והצמדה, התשכ״א–1961}}.
-- "If the violator did not pay the financial sanction on time, shekel interest and arrears fees shall be added
-- to it, for the period of the delay, until its payment, and the provisions of the Interest and Linkage Law shall
-- apply, with the necessary changes."  The two terms are defined by reference to the Interest and Linkage Law
-- (1961), whose rates and mechanics are outside the scope and are not in the sources.
-- Late: paid after the last day for payment.  A payment on the last day is on time.
@ref s.49 (src:382)
GIVEN `the day of payment` IS A DATE
      `the last day for payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49 — the payment of` `the day of payment` `is late, the last day for payment being` `the last day for payment` MEANS
    `the day of payment` GREATER THAN `the last day for payment`

-- The period of the delay: from the day after the last day for payment until the day of payment.  The
-- number of days in it (P45, kind V); the caller needs it to compute the interest.
@ref s.49 (src:382)
GIVEN `the last day for payment` IS A DATE
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 49 — the days of delay, from the day after` `the last day for payment` `until` `the day of payment` MEANS
    max 0 ((Day `the day of payment`) MINUS (Day `the last day for payment`))

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 49 — the shekel interest and the arrears fees are fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 49 — the shekel interest and the arrears fees are fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied"

-- The amount owed on a late payment: the sanction, plus the shekel interest and the arrears fees accrued over the
-- period of the delay as the Interest and Linkage Law computes them.  The caller supplies the two amounts; an
-- amount the caller does not supply is a named refusal, never zero.  A payment on time owes neither.
@ref s.49 (src:382)
GIVEN sanction IS A NUMBER
      late IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shekel interest accrued over the delay` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the arrears fees accrued over the delay` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` sanction `when the payment is late:` late `with shekel interest` `the shekel interest accrued over the delay` `and arrears fees` `the arrears fees accrued over the delay` MEANS
    IF   NOT late
    THEN sanction
    ELSE CONSIDER `the shekel interest accrued over the delay`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 49 — the shekel interest and the arrears fees are fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied`
         WHEN JUST interest THEN
             CONSIDER `the arrears fees accrued over the delay`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 49 — the shekel interest and the arrears fees are fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied`
             WHEN JUST fees THEN sanction PLUS interest PLUS fees

-- The alternative (F-INTEREST): the caller supplies RATES for the whole period of the delay, as fractions of the
-- sanction (0.01 is one per cent), and the two are added to the sanction as simple interest on the sanction alone.
-- That is this encoding's arithmetic, not the Interest and Linkage Law's.
@ref s.49 (src:382)
GIVEN sanction IS A NUMBER
      late IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shekel interest rate for the delay` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the arrears fees rate for the delay` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 49 — the amount owed, at simple rates, on a sanction of` sanction `when the payment is late:` late `with a shekel interest rate for the whole delay of` `the shekel interest rate for the delay` `and an arrears fees rate of` `the arrears fees rate for the delay` MEANS
    IF   NOT late
    THEN sanction
    ELSE CONSIDER `the shekel interest rate for the delay`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 49 — the shekel interest and the arrears fees are fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied`
         WHEN JUST interest THEN
             CONSIDER `the arrears fees rate for the delay`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 49 — the shekel interest and the arrears fees are fixed by the Interest and Linkage Law, whose rates are not in the sources, and none was supplied`
             WHEN JUST fees THEN sanction TIMES (1 PLUS interest PLUS fees)

-- s.48 and s.49 as one duty: pay within the 30 days; if not, pay the sanction together with the interest and
-- arrears fees, with no time limit (s.49 adds them "until payment").  The WITHIN is the number of days from
-- the demand to the last day; the second rung is guarded by the amount owed, a refusal when the Law's rates are
-- not supplied (so it is reached only when the deadline has passed).
@ref s.48, s.49 (src:379, src:382)
GIVEN sanction IS A NUMBER
      delivered IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
      `the shekel interest accrued over the delay` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the arrears fees accrued over the delay` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 48 to 51`
`s 48 — the violator must pay the financial sanction of` sanction `, the demand being delivered on` delivered `with` calendar `and, if late,` `the shekel interest accrued over the delay` `and` `the arrears fees accrued over the delay` MEANS
    PARTY  `the violator`
    MUST   `pay the financial sanction` `the violator` paid
           PROVIDED paid AT LEAST sanction
    WITHIN (`s 48 — the number of days from the delivery of the demand to the last day for payment` delivered calendar)
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   ( PARTY `the violator`
             MUST  `pay the financial sanction together with the interest and arrears fees` `the violator` paidLate
                   PROVIDED paidLate AT LEAST (`s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` sanction `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with shekel interest` `the shekel interest accrued over the delay` `and arrears fees` `the arrears fees accrued over the delay`)
             HENCE FULFILLED )

§§§ `s 50: payment by instalments`

-- src:386 | {{ח:סעיף|50|פריסת תשלום העיצום הכספי}}
-- src:387 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} הממונה רשאי, לבקשת המפר, להחליט על פריסת התשלום של העיצום הכספי, בהתחשב בסכום העיצום הכספי שהוטל על המפר ובנסיבות מיוחדות אחרות המצדיקות פריסה כאמור, ובלבד שמספר התשלומים לא יעלה על 12 תשלומים חודשיים.
-- src:388 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} לא שילם המפר תשלום במועדו, יראו את החלטת הממונה על פריסת התשלום כאמור בסעיף קטן (א) כבטלה, יתרת החוב תעמוד לפירעון מיידי ויחולו הוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 49|סעיף 49}}.
-- (a): "The Commissioner may, at the violator's request, decide to spread payment of the sanction, having regard to
-- the amount of the sanction imposed on the violator and to other special circumstances that justify spreading
-- it, provided the number of payments does not exceed 12 monthly payments."  The request is a fact; the
-- Commissioner's view of the amount and the circumstances is his discretion (an input); the cap is a number.
-- The number of payments is a positive whole number (a payment plan of none is no plan); the Law states only the
-- maximum.  P32, kind Q.
@ref s.50(a) (src:387)
GIVEN `the violator asked for payment by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of monthly payments` IS A NUMBER
      `the payments fall due monthly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` `the violator asked for payment by instalments` `the number of monthly payments` `the payments fall due monthly` MEANS
        "the violator's request" ... `the violator asked for payment by instalments`
    ... "monthly payments" ... `the payments fall due monthly`
    ... "at least one payment" ... `the number of monthly payments` AT LEAST 1
    AND "not more than 12" ... `the number of monthly payments` AT MOST 12

@ref s.50(a) (src:387)
GIVEN `the violator asked for payment by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of monthly payments` IS A NUMBER
      `the payments fall due monthly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner finds that the amount and special circumstances justify spreading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 48 to 51`
`s 50(a) — the Commissioner may allow payment by instalments` `the violator asked for payment by instalments` `the number of monthly payments` `the payments fall due monthly` `the Commissioner finds that the amount and special circumstances justify spreading` MEANS
    IF       `s 50(a) — an instalment plan is within what the Law allows` `the violator asked for payment by instalments` `the number of monthly payments` `the payments fall due monthly`
         AND `the Commissioner finds that the amount and special circumstances justify spreading`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `allow payment of the financial sanction by instalments` `the Commissioner`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (b): "If the violator did not pay a payment on time, the Commissioner's decision on spreading shall be treated as
-- void, the balance of the debt shall fall due at once, and s.49 shall apply."
@ref s.50(b) (src:388)
GIVEN `a payment was not made when it fell due` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50(b) — the decision on instalments is treated as void and the balance falls due at once` `a payment was not made when it fell due` MEANS
    `a payment was not made when it fell due`

@ref s.50(b) (src:388)
GIVEN `the sanction` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid so far` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 50(b) — the balance of the debt that falls due at once on a sanction of` `the sanction` `of which` `the amount paid so far` `has been paid` MEANS
    max 0 (`the sanction` MINUS `the amount paid so far`)

§§§ `s 51: collection (inert)`

-- src:390 | {{ח:סעיף|51|גבייה}}
-- src:391 | {{ח:ת}} עיצום כספי ייגבה לאוצר המדינה, ועל גבייתו יחול {{ח:חיצוני|חוק המרכז לגביית קנסות, אגרות והוצאות|חוק המרכז לגביית קנסות, אגרות והוצאות, התשנ״ה–1995}}.
-- "A financial sanction shall be collected for the State Treasury, and its collection shall be governed by the
-- Fines, Fees and Expenses Collection Centre Law, 5755-1995."  Neither limb produces a decision this encoding
-- can compute: the destination of the money is carried as the constant below, and the Collection Centre Law is
-- outside the scope.
@ref s.51 (src:391)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 51 — the payee of a financial sanction` MEANS "the State Treasury"
